From the speculative and alternative thoughts, the possibility of desire arises. 27. Meaning of the word:
From the ego of the Vaikarika-Sattva; from being distorted; Manah-- Mind; Tatvam-- Rule; Ajayat-- Unborn;
Happened; Yat-- Of which; Sankalp-- Thoughts; Vikalpabhyam-- From such alternatives; Vartate-- Occurs; Kama-Sambhavah--
The rise of desire.. From this, the mind arises, due to which
the desire arises from resolutions and alternatives.
Meaning: The characteristics of the mind are resolutions and alternatives, which arise due to various kinds of desires. We desire what suits our sense of pleasure, and
we exclude what seems adverse. Our mind does not remain stable, but if
we engage in the activities of Krishna consciousness (devotion), then that same mind becomes stable.
Otherwise, when
the mind remains in a physical state, it keeps fluctuating, and all this resolve-
option is unreal or perishable. It is said that one whose mind is not stable in Krishna consciousness
keeps wandering between resolve and option. No matter how much a person advances in educational qualifications,
until he is stable in Krishna consciousness, he will
resolve and option, and will not be able to stabilize the mind in any subject. Yadvidudniruddhakhyam Hashikanadhi Shcharam.
